/*
 * pb_map.h - density map for the Particle Buddha view (CyberCycle anim 3).
 *
 * 64x64 unsigned bytes, bilinear-sampled up to the 128x128 screen. Each value
 * is the relative odds of a particle being at that spot: 255 at the third eye
 * between the brows, 0 in the eye sockets, the nostrils and the mouth line.
 *
 * Not hand-drawn and not a picture of a face - it was fitted numerically so
 * that the running animation *time-averages* to the reference clip. Particles
 * drift outward and smear, so the map is pre-compensated for that smear and
 * looks slightly sharper than the face you actually see on screen. The fit is
 * driven by the real firmware renderer, so it tracks PB_BIG0/PB_BIG1 and the
 * rest of the constants - change those and this table wants regenerating.
 *
 * A radial floor is folded in as a maximum (not a sum): zero across the whole
 * face, rising smoothly past mid-radius to about 9/255 at the corners. Without
 * it the fitted density near the edges sits below PB_DIE and particles wink out
 * before they can be drawn, leaving a dead margin around the screen.
 *
 * Generated - edit the fitting script, not this table.
 */
